  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the numerator using the power rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n{({7}^{2})}^{4}={7}^{2\\cdot 4}={7}^{8}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{7}^{8}}{{7}^{3}}={7}^{8-3}={7}^{5}\n$$",
